# Don't stop here, keep learning!

## Additional Resources
* <a href="https://www.teachai.org/" target="_blank">TeachAI.org</a> Empowering educators to teach with and about AI.
* <a href="https://www.teachai.org/ailiteracy" target="_blank">AILit Framework</a> from TeachAI.org.
* <a href="https://code.org/en-US/artificial-intelligence" target="_blank">AI Curriculum Resources</a> from Code.org.
* <a href="https://aipedagogy.org/assignments/" target="_blank">AI Assignments</a> from AI Pedagogy Project.

## Take it Further Activities

Want to learn more? Try out the following optional activities.
  <!-- Dropdown 1 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	AI Literacy Skills
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Does your state or district have AI Literacy Skills or Standards? Search online to see if you can find them, and take the time to read them over. How do they compare to the AILit Framework you learned about in this module?
</p>
</details>

  <!-- Dropdown 2 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	AI-Integrated Project
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Take the idea of designing with AI in mind to the next level by creating your own AI-Integrated project that not only encourages the use of AI, but includes using AI as part of the learning objectives.<br><br>Feel free to modify an existing project or start fresh.
</p>

</div>

</details>

